IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cyp-youth-court`

-- Children and Young Persons Act 1993, Part 3, ss 36, 38, 39, 42, 44 and 49 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved). Expected results were written by hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`Jun Hao's shop theft charge` MEANS Charge WITH
    `age at the start of the hearing` IS 15
    `triable only by the High Court` IS FALSE
    `Public Prosecutor applies for Youth Court trial` IS FALSE
    `legal representative consents` IS FALSE
    `Second Schedule or repeat similar offence` IS FALSE
    `transmitted on fiat or by the court's own motion` IS FALSE
    `charged jointly with an adult` IS FALSE

`Jun Hao at fifteen, first offence` MEANS Offender WITH
    `age on the day of the finding` IS 15
    `previously sent to a juvenile rehabilitation centre` IS FALSE
    `too unruly for a JRC or place of detention` IS FALSE
    `court satisfied reformative training is needed` IS FALSE

`a fifteen-year-old the court would send to RTC, no history` MEANS Offender WITH
    `age on the day of the finding` IS 15
    `previously sent to a juvenile rehabilitation centre` IS FALSE
    `too unruly for a JRC or place of detention` IS FALSE
    `court satisfied reformative training is needed` IS TRUE

