§ `REQ-0266 (Jun Hao j023) -- a fifteen-year-old charged with shop theft`

-- s 39(1): tried by the Youth Court (theft is not High Court-only, he is below 16 so s 39(2A) cannot apply, no adult co-accused).
#ASSERT `the court that tries the charge` `Jun Hao's shop theft charge` EQUALS `the Youth Court`

-- s 49(1): on proof or admission, orders (a) to (j) are open to him; probation is (e).
#ASSERT `the order is available on proof of the offence` `probation order` `Jun Hao at fifteen, first offence`
#ASSERT `the order is available on proof of the offence` `discharge` `Jun Hao at fifteen, first offence`
#ASSERT `the order is available on proof of the offence` `community service order` `Jun Hao at fifteen, first offence`
#ASSERT `the order is available on proof of the offence` `juvenile rehabilitation centre` `Jun Hao at fifteen, first offence`
#ASSERT `the order is available on proof of the offence` `fine, damages or costs` `Jun Hao at fifteen, first offence`

-- s 49(1)(k): reformative training is not open to a 15-year-old with no JRC history who is not too unruly.
#ASSERT NOT `the order is available on proof of the offence` `reformative training` `Jun Hao at fifteen, first offence`

-- s 44(3): orders on the parent without recording a finding of guilt -- damages, costs or security, but not a fine.
#ASSERT `the order may be made without recording a finding of guilt` `parent gives security for good behaviour`
#ASSERT NOT `the order may be made without recording a finding of guilt` `parent pays a fine`

-- s 42(2): no imprisonment at 15 unless certified unruly.
#ASSERT NOT `section 42 permits imprisonment` 15 FALSE FALSE

§ `s 36 -- arrest`

#ASSERT `an arrested person not released must be brought before a Youth Court` 15
#ASSERT `the latest time in hours to bring the arrested person before a Magistrate` EQUALS 48
#ASSERT `the arrested person is to be released on a bond` `no section 36 circumstance`
#ASSERT NOT `the arrested person is to be released on a bond` `likely to abscond only`

§ `s 38 -- advisers`

#ASSERT `the advisers the judge must sit with` TRUE FALSE EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the advisers the judge must sit with` TRUE TRUE EQUALS 0

§ `s 39 -- which court`

#ASSERT `the court that tries the charge` `a seventeen-year-old on a High Court-only charge` EQUALS `the General Division of the High Court`
#ASSERT `the court that tries the charge` `the same charge, Prosecutor applies and lawyer consents` EQUALS `the Youth Court`
#ASSERT `the court that tries the charge` `a sixteen-year-old robbery charge sent on fiat` EQUALS `another court of appropriate jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `the court that tries the charge` `a sixteen-year-old robbery charge kept by the Youth Court` EQUALS `the Youth Court`
#ASSERT `the court that tries the charge` `a fifteen-year-old robbery charge with a fiat` EQUALS `the Youth Court`
#ASSERT `the court that tries the charge` `a fifteen-year-old charged jointly with a twenty-year-old` EQUALS `another court of appropriate jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `the court that tries the charge` `an offence at seventeen, hearing starting at eighteen` EQUALS `another court of appropriate jurisdiction`

§ `s 42 -- imprisonment and corporal punishment`

#ASSERT NOT `section 42 permits imprisonment` 13 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 42 permits imprisonment` 15 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 42 permits imprisonment` 17 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 42 permits corporal punishment` 15 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `section 42 permits corporal punishment` 17 FALSE TRUE

§ `s 44(1) -- the parent pays`

#ASSERT `the fine must be ordered against the parent` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the fine must be ordered against the parent` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the fine must be ordered against the parent` TRUE TRUE

§ `s 49(1)(k) -- reformative training`

#ASSERT NOT `reformative training is available` `a fifteen-year-old the court would send to RTC, no history`
#ASSERT `reformative training is available` `a fifteen-year-old previously sent to a JRC`
#ASSERT `reformative training is available` `an eighteen-year-old at the finding`

§ `s 49(1), (3) -- limits`

#ASSERT `the probation period is within section 49(1)(e)` 6
#ASSERT NOT `the probation period is within section 49(1)(e)` 5
#ASSERT NOT `the community service is within section 49(1)(f)` 241
#ASSERT `the maximum detention in months under section 49(1)(g)` TRUE EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the maximum detention in months under section 49(1)(g)` FALSE EQUALS 6
#ASSERT NOT `the weekend detention is within section 49(1)(h)` 27

§ `s 49(2) -- combinations`

#ASSERT `the two orders may be combined under section 49(2)` `probation order` `community service order`
#ASSERT `the two orders may be combined under section 49(2)` `probation order` `detention in a place of detention`
#ASSERT NOT `the two orders may be combined under section 49(2)` `detention in a place of detention` `community service order`
#ASSERT NOT `the two orders may be combined under section 49(2)` `juvenile rehabilitation centre` `probation order`
#ASSERT NOT `the two orders may be combined under section 49(2)` `discharge` `fine, damages or costs`
